WEBVTT

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.120
Excuse me.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.240
Is Shamon-san here?

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.250
Um, hi...

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.000
Huh?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.090
Um, excuse me.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:56.260
If you have any business here,
you can tell me.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.430
I'm the chief clerk, Mataji.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.800
Please come this way.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.480
Strange rumors seem to be circulating,
and it's causing trouble for us.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.640
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.150
And are you sure the priest knows you?

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.110
Yeah, he sure does.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:15.990
I'm sorry.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.900
I don't have an ulterior motive,

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.120
but your appearance is a bit unusual.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.490
No, we're used to it, so you don't have to worry.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.500
What the hell is this?

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.800
That was Heihachi-san and a demon.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.010
What's wrong, Toki?

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.260
Was it him again?!

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.740
That's enough.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.330
If you go any further, you'll become unclean.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.870
Human blood and continuing hatred will make you lose your reason.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.580
Do you want to become like that before you meet your master?

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.590
I can't stop my body from disintegrating.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.090
Yakou-dono gave me this power, this impurity.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.850
Impurity can also provide
enormous power to demons.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.180
You idiot.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.860
It's a charm.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.490
It will at least help
you to keep your shape.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.240
Use it.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.020
You don't seem so bad.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.030
If it's just this, I can cure you.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:27.160
You were interesting for a human,

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.040
but I don't think we'll ever meet again.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.710
Good-bye, Heihachi.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.040
Wait.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:42.050
I still have something to tell you.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.300
Damned simpleton!

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:51.180
Giving away the cloth
on which I wrote the spell.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.640
He doesn't think about the consequences.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.060
U-Um, I thought so,
but was that really bad for him?

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.360
I don't know.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.740
It means that he'll eventually just disappear.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.860
I-Isn't that bad?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.450
Just shut up!

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.330
Utsubushi! Susutake.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.950
That idiot is in Nihonbashi.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:11.620
We have to hurry.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.790
Do you know that area?

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.120
Yeah, you can count on me.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.380
Okay, then take us there.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.630
Utsubushi, fly.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.840
I don't mind that, but how
many do I have to carry?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:33.850
Okay, okay. I'll take everyone.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:40.360
Do you know a Rikugou Tokidoki?

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.400
Really, you know Toki?!

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:47.110
If he's involved, it will be dangerous,
so I have to be prepared.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.030
Then Tsuyukusa also...

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.120
Well, I don't think he'll be unkind to us.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:56.250
That left eye of his must've seen what I saw.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:02.130
Babysit Tsuyukusa until I arrive, Rikugou.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.720
By the way, I don't think
I introduced myself earlier.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.220
I'm called Heihachi.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.180
Nice to meet you.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.060
I'm Tsuyukusa.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.060
You didn't have to be nice.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:21.860
Tsuyukusa.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.950
Hey, you!

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.370
This is Nakamura-ya, right?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.620
Kuchiha!

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.130
Are you an exorcist?

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.470
Why does a demon like you
have business here?!

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.930
Depending on your answer,
I may really kill you this time!

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.640
Smells like a dog.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.480
Oh, are you a mixed blood?

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:02.980
A wolf becomes just a dog,
if she's raised by humans.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:08.990
What a pity you can't smell
that I'm on a different level.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.240
Kuchiha!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.330
How can I lose to a mere demon?!

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.540
Don't play with me!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.910
You're annoying!

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.870
Stop it, Tsuyukusa!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.590
How do you know my name?

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.600
I think it'd be quicker
to ask Bonten about that.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.730
Are you the Blank Page?!

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.980
Toki, Kuchiha, run!

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.030
Get in the house!

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.030
Quickly!

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:36.450
Shamon-san.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:37.490
You get in there too!

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:45.040
You damned priest.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.580
Damn it!

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.040
My special rosary didn't work.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.760
Hey, come on.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.050
Priest,

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:55.550
tell this to that boy.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:59.560
If you don't run away,
I won't treat you specially.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:04.980
If you don't want to die,
you'd better leave too,

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.860
before you're swallowed by my hatred.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.570
Was that about Tokidoki?

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.780
What are you doing?
Who the hell was that?

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:18.910
Kuchiha.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.790
Are you making a joke,
crossing swords here?

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:29.590
What will you do if people
in the street heard that racket?

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:31.880
Didn't I say we're in trouble?

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.550
I shouldn't have let you in here.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.800
Could you please be quiet!

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.840
That was a demon.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.550
She drove it off!

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:41.510
Huh?

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.810
What are you talking about?
That was just a brat.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.480
Are you three in league with the priest?

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:53.030
You say there's a demon and make a fuss to get money. Am I wrong?

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.740
Hold on. That's nonsense!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.860
I shouldn't have depended on a priest like him, even if I was impatient.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.120
What if officers come here
because we consulted a priest?

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.490
And in addition, there was that fight...

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:05.750
Are you worried about an official investigation?

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.500
That really <i>was a demon,</i>

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.250
and it was quite a powerful one.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.300
Are you two all right?

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.760
As I said, it looked just like a human.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.840
How on earth could that be a demon?

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:20.970
Didn't I say it was powerful?

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:24.640
The base appearance of demons
is incorporeal.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.730
I don't think you'd normally
be able to see them.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:29.480
They are more like spirits than humans.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:32.230
Those demons that are closest
to humans and to reality

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.980
are the most difficult to deal with.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.440
What on earth did you do

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.200
to incur the anger of one of those?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.990
I-I don't know anything.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:45.740
What about that big tree
trunk in the warehouse?

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:51.210
W-We bought that from a timber dealer
in Naitou-Shinjuku,

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.710
and we'll give it to a craftsman who lives behind our store.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:56.710
Then do you know what this is?

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.890
Isn't this what you really wanted to buy?

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.430
Isn't this a prohibited drug, opium?

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.640
Opium?

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.230
I don't know how you incurred
the anger of the demons,

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.980
but you're about to incur
the anger of a lot of people.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.270
A-Anyone!

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.360
There are robbers here! Capture them!

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.360
What's going on, chief clerk?

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.860
It's a break-in! Help me!

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.200
What a fearless guy!

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.580
Get him!

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.450
This is not what I expected.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.500
Should I kill them?

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.910
No, you mustn't, Kuchiha!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:33.830
Lock them in the warehouse.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.500
Ouch.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.140
Stay there for a while.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.730
Could you tell us one thing?

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.360
Are you the one who injured the owner?

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:56.110
How could it be me?

00:11:56.110 --> 00:12:00.360
I'm a businessman, but I never hurt people.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.490
I suppose so,

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.870
because there must be witnesses.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.450
Shamon-sama.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.080
Weren't you here to exterminate demons?

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:10.540
Yeah.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:13.170
I know the owner quite well.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.130
Strange things have been
happening in the store.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:19.380
I was worried that the customers were getting more unruly.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:23.380
I heard that someone was burned quite horribly in the warehouse, where a fire couldn't occur.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.890
That's strange.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:28.180
So I was brought here.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:32.390
In fact, there were many small monsters in the main building,

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:36.400
but there weren't any in the warehouse, where the incident occurred.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.070
I couldn't figure out why the fire broke out.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:40.480
Huh?

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.900
So I searched here and there,
and I found that.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.320
That's the tree trunk.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.910
It's heavily scorched, isn't it?

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:53.870
Yeah. So I thought the fire started there,

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:55.920
but instead of demons,
I found something else.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:58.130
The opium.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.800
Then this warehouse must be safe, right?

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:02.760
Yeah.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.930
But I think you should cover your mouth and nose with a cloth.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:10.930
That bag of opium was torn open, and the powder is spreading.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.770
We have to find a way out quickly.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:16.440
Now answer honestly, Toki.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.560
Who was that kid?

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:19.940
You know him, right?

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.690
No, it's not really like that.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:30.910
Babysit Tsuyukusa until I arrive, Rikugou.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:35.620
If Bonten has done something to my left eye...

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:40.460
I'm not going to ask for details now,
but can't you stop him?

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:45.170
I'd guess that the chief clerk will bring an officer he's got connections with.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:48.260
He won't let us out until then.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.100
That's bad.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.720
That demon will come back soon.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.390
And if we're locked up in this place,

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:56.690
we can't protect ourselves.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.150
Someone might die.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:10.240
Imayou, I found it.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:12.410
Thank you.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.290
Oh, you've been injured.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.870
It's no big deal.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:19.750
Can you stand?

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.250
Yes.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:26.760
Damn it. It's tough working with just half of Bon's written charm.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.260
No.

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.010
I'm all right.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:34.260
Until I get Master back, I won't disappear.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.310
Tsuyukusa...

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:42.610
You are my master.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.860
In other words, you are my parent.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.280
The contract of a demon is absolute.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:51.030
I won't disappear and leave you.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:56.370
Honestly, you guys are idiots.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:06.340
If there were any way to restore the old relationship...

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.260
Hey, Imayou, let's go.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.050
This should put an end to the nightmare.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:20.770
...that I had with you...

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.860
This is your last night.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.410
Won't it open?

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.410
Come down, Kuchiha.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:42.080
Okay.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:51.930
Now there's nothing we can do.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:54.510
We're lucky that it's spring.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.560
The powder here is making us thirsty.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.100
If it were summer, we might die.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.270
Right.

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:14.490
Um, that growling sound was definitely Kuchiha's stomach.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.950
Yeah, I'm hungry too.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:46.150
You've grown.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:49.940
You mean I'm fat?

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:52.900
Um, that could be, but...

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:55.240
Just joking.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.410
I was just comparing to your childhood.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:01.410
Oh, I've got it.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:05.370
Um, no. I was just reminded of a friend.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.750
May I ask you who he is?

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.920
Sure, that's why I'm reminded
of him these days.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:16.180
He was more like a brother than a friend.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.930
He taught me both good things and bad things.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:22.890
To others, he probably looked like a brute.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:27.150
He was a bit like Shamon-sama... to me.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:30.400
No matter how I abused him,

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:31.780
I could go back there.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:32.940
He was my family.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:38.490
Master! Master!

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:41.030
Come now, Imayou.

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:52.210
If that were taken away,
even a demon would surely get angry.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:55.220
What do you mean?

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.010
Are you talking about that demon we met?

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:00.180
Um, no, it's not about him.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:06.940
They wouldn't understand if I said that I saw
a fox demon and Heihachi with my left eye.

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:08.520
I-It's nothing.

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:12.020
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:16.280
But if demons have emotions too, they might try
to avenge the death of someone precious to them.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:20.240
I hear that foxes are especially emotional.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.240
Enemies create more enemies.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.490
Hatred brings more hatred.

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:27.500
This flow of misfortune might not differ between humans and demons.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.710
Then all we have to do is exterminate demons.

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:33.250
What caused them doesn't matter.

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.050
If they retreat, that's fine.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:37.470
If they stand against Shamon-sama,
they're the enemy.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:41.220
If they're human, I'll strike with the blunt edge.
If demons, I'll kill with my blade.

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.720
That is demon hunting.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.270
Kuchiha.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:52.520
Revenge. Eat the humans!

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:55.480
I really miss that one.

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:58.740
I get sad again when I think about his regrets.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.820
Gather, gather, compatriots.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:04.410
Throng to the one who has my master.

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:07.660
Scrawl inside the dark forever.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.670
Now let us go on a journey to death.

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:15.130
Leave the dwelling fox behind at
the decayed tree deep in the mountains.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:18.010
Go to the town where it's flat
and no sacred trees grow.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.260
And now, I will become a god!

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:22.260
Here they come!

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.750
Where is it? Where is it?

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:52.170
Where did you hide it?

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.290
Find my master's trunk!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.670
Hey, where's the water? You're late!

00:19:58.670 --> 00:19:59.300
Huh?

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:02.180
Wh-What? What's up?

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:04.430
Hey, hang on!

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:08.890
Where did you hide it, little rabbit?

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.730
Present it to Amaza!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.020
Wh-Who the hell are you?

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:16.900
The trunk where the fox spirit dwelled...

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.030
Where did you hide it?

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:23.950
Trunk? I-If you're talking about timber,

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:26.450
w-we keep all the timber
we bought in the warehouse.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:29.290
It's over there.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.540
It's over there!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:35.040
I will reward the one who finds it!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:37.000
Hurry and go.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:40.590
They're coming toward us!

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.850
If they can't get in,

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:54.020
they must still be mostly incorporeal.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:58.230
The people in the store are also in danger!

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:03.570
However, we can't see anything.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:09.450
Uniformly distributed particulates.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:14.580
Dryness from the dehumidifying
effect of charcoal.

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:18.630
Oxygen!

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:23.050
I heard that someone was burned quite horribly in the warehouse, where a fire couldn't occur.

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:26.640
I don't know why the fire broke out.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:32.600
Is it possible?

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.600
Lie down, you two!
